 {'type':'clarification','text':'The source prints 88 − 54 = 35; the arithmetic is 34 miles. For an actual decrement from t = 1.5 to t = 1.0, the signed change is f(1.0) − f(1.5) = 54 − 88 = −34 miles. The positive 34 is the magnitude of that change. For the increment from 1.5 to 2.0, the signed change is correctly 32 miles.'}
