 {'type':'clarification','text':r'The finite table suggests the trend; the limit proves it. For P at x = 0.5 and Q at x = 0.5 + Δx, \(\frac{(0.5+\Delta x)^2-0.25}{\Delta x}=1+\Delta x\) for Δx ≠ 0. Thus the secant slopes tend to 1 as Δx → 0. The tangent line through P is \(y-0.25=x-0.5\), or y = x − 0.25.'}
