EXAMPLES.append({'id':'we-3-source-2','num':'2','title':'Example 2','problem':r'The height of corn t days after germination is \(h(t)=\sqrt t-1\), t ≥ 1. (a) Find its average growth rate. (b) Find the average growth rate between days 4 and 9.','given':'Height h(t) = √t − 1; t ≥ 1.','method':'Form a difference quotient, then use t = 4 and Δt = 5.','steps':[r'For Δt ≠ 0 with t and t + Δt in the domain, the average rate is \(\frac{h(t+\Delta t)-h(t)}{\Delta t}\).',r'Substitute and cancel the constants: \(\frac{\sqrt{t+\Delta t}-1-(\sqrt t-1)}{\Delta t}=\frac{\sqrt{t+\Delta t}-\sqrt t}{\Delta t}\).',r'Optionally multiply by the conjugate to obtain \(\frac{1}{\sqrt{t+\Delta t}+\sqrt t}\). This is an equivalent average-rate formula.',r'For days 4 to 9, t = 4 and Δt = 9 − 4 = 5. Heights are h(4) = 1 and h(9) = 2.',r'The average growth rate is \(\frac{2-1}{9-4}=\frac15\) height unit per day. This is an interval average, not the instantaneous rate at every day in the interval.'],'answer':r'(a) \(\frac{\sqrt{t+\Delta t}-\sqrt t}{\Delta t}=\frac{1}{\sqrt{t+\Delta t}+\sqrt t}\). (b) 1/5 height unit per day.','solutionBlocks':[{'type':'diagram','caption':'SpaceBook learning graph — Example 2','diagram':CORN}],'progressiveSolution':True,'solutionOrigin':'SpaceBook learning enhancement','sourceReferences':[{'pageStart':65,'pageEnd':66,'verification':'complete question and solution visually compared with JPG and full PDF'}]})
