 heading('Example 10 — solution'),paragraph(r'a. If \(y=f(x)=(4x-3)^3=u^3\) with u = 4x − 3, then, the first derivative w.r.t. x by chain rule is:'),command(None,r'\(\frac{dy}{dx}=\frac{dy}{du}\frac{du}{dx}=\frac{d}{du}(u^3)\frac{d}{dx}(4x-3)=(3u^2)(4)=12u^2=12(4x-3)^2,\quad u=4x-3\)'),paragraph(r'b. If \(y=f(x)=\sqrt{15x^2+1}=\sqrt{u}=u^{\frac12}\) with u = 15x² + 1, then, the first derivative by chain rule is:'),command(None,r'\(\frac{dy}{dx}=\frac{dy}{du}\frac{du}{dx},\quad u=15x^2+1\)'),command(None,r'\(=\frac{d}{du}(u^{\frac12})\frac{d}{dx}(15x^2+1)=\frac12u^{-\frac12}(30x)=\frac{15x}{\sqrt{u}}=\frac{15x}{\sqrt{15x^2+1}}\)'),
 heading('Example 11'),paragraph(r'The revenue realized by a small city from the collection of fines from parking tickets is given by \(R(x)=\frac{8000x}{x+2}\), where x is the number of work hours each day that can be devoted to parking patrol. At the outbreak of a flu epidemic, 30 work hours are used daily in parking patrol, but during the epidemic that number is decreasing at the rate of 6 work hours per day. How fast is revenue from parking fines decreasing during the epidemic?'),heading('Solution'),paragraph(r'We need to find \(\frac{dR}{dt}\), the change in revenue with respect to time t. The chain rule is used to obtain dR/dt.'),command(None,r'\(\frac{dR}{dt}=\frac{dR}{dx}\frac{dx}{dt}\)','i'),paragraph('First find dR/dx as follows.'),command(None,r"\(R'(x)=\frac{dR}{dx}=\frac{(x+2)(8000)-8000x(1)}{(x+2)^2}=\frac{16000}{(x+2)^2}\)"),command(None,r"\(R'(30)=\frac{16000}{(30+2)^2}=15.625,\quad\text{at }x=30\)"),paragraph('dR/dx = 15.625 and dx/dt = −6 are used in equation (i) to obtain:'),command(None,r'\(\frac{dR}{dt}=\frac{dR}{dx}\frac{dx}{dt}=(15.625)(-6)=-93.75\)'),paragraph(r'This tells us that the revenue is being lost at the rate of approximately \(\text{\$94}\) per day.'),
 {'type':'clarification','text':r'The calculation is instantaneous at the initial level x = 30. At another time the rate is −96000/(x + 2)², with the current x. If x(t) = 30 − 6t and t is measured in days, the model is physically meaningful only while x ≥ 0 (0 ≤ t ≤ 5). The question does not explicitly give currency units, although its solution uses dollars. Revenue decreases at 93.75 revenue units per day initially, or $93.75 per day under that dollar interpretation.'},
