EXAMPLES.append({'id':'we-3-source-12','num':'12','title':'Example 12','problem':r'Verify dy/dx = 1/(dx/dy) for (a) y = (4x − 3)³ and (b) \(y=\sqrt{15x^2+1}\), wherever the inverse derivatives exist.','given':'The functions from Example 10; the inverse relation has additional restrictions.','method':'Find actual inverse branches, differentiate them, then compare with the forward derivatives.','steps':[r'(a) Solve y = (4x − 3)³ to obtain \(x=\frac{\text{∛y}+3}4\). This inverse exists for all real y.',r'For y ≠ 0, differentiating the inverse gives dx/dy = 1/[12(∛y)²]. Substituting ∛y = 4x − 3 yields dx/dy = 1/[12(4x − 3)²].',r'Take its reciprocal: 1/(dx/dy) = 12(4x − 3)² = dy/dx, for x ≠ 3/4.',r'At x = 3/4, y = 0 and dy/dx = 0. The inverse difference quotient is (∛h)/(4h) = 1/[4(∛h)²], unbounded as h → 0. No finite dx/dy exists there.',r'(b) Squaring yields x² = (y² − 1)/15. On the positive branch x = √((y² − 1)/15); on the negative branch x = −√((y² − 1)/15). Each inverse branch uses y > 1 for differentiation.',r'For the positive branch, dx/dy = y/[√15 √(y² − 1)]. Since √(y² − 1) = √15 x, this is y/(15x).',r'For the negative branch the inverse derivative has a minus sign; using x < 0 gives the same formula dx/dy = y/(15x).',r'Therefore \(\frac1{dx/dy}=\frac{15x}{y}=\frac{15x}{\sqrt{15x^2+1}}=\frac{dy}{dx}\), for x ≠ 0 on the chosen branch.',r'At x = 0, y = 1 and the forward derivative is zero. The inverse branches have unbounded one-sided slopes at y = 1, so the finite reciprocal relation does not apply there.'],'answer':r'(a) Verified for x ≠ 3/4. (b) Verified on either x > 0 or x < 0 branch. The forward derivatives are \(12(4x-3)^2\) and \(\frac{15x}{\sqrt{15x^2+1}}\); the excluded points have no finite inverse derivative.','sourceClarification':'The printed verification substitutes reciprocals without independently deriving an inverse. The learning solution calculates the inverse branches and explains zero-derivative exceptions.','progressiveSolution':True,'solutionOrigin':'SpaceBook learning enhancement','sourceReferences':[{'page':79,'jpg':'044_page_1.jpg','verification':'complete question and source solution visually compared with JPG and full PDF'}]})

